```python
        line = sys.stdin.readline()
        if line.endswith('\n'):
            line = line[:-1]
        if line.endswith('\r'):
            line = line[:-1]
        if not line or line[0] not in ('y', 'Y'):
            raise OSError(f"not writing to '{dst}' (user declined)")
```

This checks the very first character of the input (after removing only trailing line terminators) without stripping leading whitespace, so `" y"`, `" Y"`, `"  y"`, etc. all correctly decline.

